    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on a targeted pursuit of stolen bases and exploitable matchups against lower-tier pitching. **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) headlines our daily projections, benefiting from a soft matchup against Klassen (6.12 xERA). His elite platoon advantage and top-tier lineup spot make him our highest-scoring play, offering the most reliable floor for production. While the raw score for **Mickey Moniak** (66.02) is bolstered significantly by a +14% park factor against Lauer, he remains a high-variance play due to the negative platoon split. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** (65.40) and **Seiya Suzuki** (60.01) represent our primary offensive engine; both receive a \"SB efficiency\" bump due to their opponents\u2019 slow deliveries, which is essential given our aggressive strategy to close the gap in the league\u2019s scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (41.70), who barely missed the cut. While he possesses the talent to outperform his mark, the combination of a difficult SP_xERA and a sharp negative platoon hit caused his efficiency to crater just below our active threshold. We are taking a cautious approach with **Josh Naylor** (44.09) and **Griffin Conine** (41.36); both are hovering near the danger zone due to tough SP matchups against Harrison and Wheeler, respectively. **Griffin Conine** specifically faces an elite defensive catcher, which limits his upside today. We will monitor the weather reports for any late-breaking developments, but the priority remains deploying **Brice Turang** at the top of the order to capitalize on his elite speed-to-base-path efficiency. All other bench assets, including **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**, remain sidelined as they fail to cross our 40.0 efficiency floor.",
